<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="generator" content="{{ tool.name }} {{ tool.version }}">
  <title>{{ report_title }} — {{ investigation.hostname }}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f4f6f8;
      --panel: #ffffff;
      --ink: #1a202c;
      --muted: #5b6777;
      --line: #d9e0e8;
      --accent: #123b5d;
      --accent-soft: #e8f0f7;
      --critical: #b3123b;
      --high: #d9480f;
      --medium: #b7791f;
      --low: #2b6cb0;
      --info: #4a5568;
      --ok: #2f855a;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--ink);
      font: 14px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    }
    a { color: var(--accent); }
    .page { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 22px 60px; }
    header.hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f2c45 0%, #164b72 62%, #1f6b8f 100%);
      color: #fff;
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 30px 32px;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(15, 44, 69, .22);
    }
    header.hero h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: .2px; }
    header.hero .sub { color: #d6e6f2; font-size: 14px; }
    .hero-grid { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px 40px; margin-top: 20px; }
    .hero-item { min-width: 180px; }
    .hero-item .label { color: #b9d2e4; font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .8px; }
    .hero-item .value { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; word-break: break-word; }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block; padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .4px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff;
    }
    .badge.severity-critical { background: var(--critical); }
    .badge.severity-high { background: var(--high); }
    .badge.severity-medium { background: var(--medium); }
    .badge.severity-low { background: var(--low); }
    .badge.severity-informational { background: var(--info); }
    .badge.status-ok { background: var(--ok); }
    .badge.status-partial { background: var(--medium); }
    .badge.status-error { background: var(--critical); }
    .badge.status-skipped { background: var(--info); }
    .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin: 22px 0; }
    .card {
      background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(26, 32, 44, .04);
    }
    .card .k { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .7px; }
    .card .v { font-size: 25px; font-weight: 750; margin-top: 4px; }
    .card .h { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 2px; }
    .risk-card { border-left: 5px solid {{ risk.rating | rating_color }}; }
    .risk-card .v { color: {{ risk.rating | rating_color }}; }
    section { margin-top: 30px; }
    section > h2 {
      font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 12px; padding-bottom: 7px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);
      letter-spacing: .2px;
    }
    .panel { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    .small { font-size: 12px; }
    .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
    .callout { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); padding: 13px 16px; border-radius: 6px; }
    .callout.warn { border-left-color: var(--medium); background: #fdf6e7; }
    .callout.danger { border-left-color: var(--critical); background: #fbeaef; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
    th, td { text-align: left; padding: 9px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
    th { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .6px; background: #f8fafc; }
    tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
    .finding {
      background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 5px solid var(--info);
      border-radius: 9px; margin-bottom: 12px; overflow: hidden;
    }
    .finding.severity-critical { border-left-color: var(--critical); }
    .finding.severity-high { border-left-color: var(--high); }
    .finding.severity-medium { border-left-color: var(--medium); }
    .finding.severity-low { border-left-color: var(--low); }
    .finding summary {
      cursor: pointer; list-style: none; padding: 14px 16px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 8px 14px; align-items: baseline;
    }
    .finding summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .finding .title { font-weight: 650; flex: 1 1 420px; }
    .finding .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
    .finding .body { padding: 0 16px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .finding .body h4 { margin: 14px 0 5px; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .6px; color: var(--muted); }
    .finding .body p { margin: 4px 0; }
    pre {
      background: #0f1b26; color: #dce7f1; padding: 13px 15px; border-radius: 7px;
      overflow: auto; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45;
    }
    code { background: #eef2f6; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 12px; }
    .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin: 4px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .chips li { background: #eef2f6; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 2px 9px; font-size: 11px; }
    .integrity-ok { color: var(--ok); font-weight: 650; }
    .integrity-bad { color: var(--critical); font-weight: 650; }
    footer { margin-top: 34px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 16px; }
    @media print {
      body { background: #fff; }
      .page { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
      header.hero { box-shadow: none; border-radius: 0; }
      .finding, .panel, .card { break-inside: avoid; }
      .finding[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>{{ report_title }}</h1>
    <div class="sub">
      Host <strong>{{ investigation.hostname }}</strong> ·
      Generated {{ investigation.generated_at }} ·
      {{ tool.name }} v{{ tool.version }}
    </div>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-item">
        <div class="label">Investigation</div>
        <div class="value mono">{{ investigation.id }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-item">
        <div class="label">Risk rating</div>
        <div class="value">{{ risk.rating }} <span class="small">({{ risk.score }}/100)</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-item">
        <div class="label">Overall severity</div>
        <div class="value"><span class="badge severity-{{ risk.overall_severity }}">{{ risk.overall_severity }}</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-item">
        <div class="label">Mode</div>
        <div class="value">{{ investigation.mode | default("read-only") }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card risk-card">
      <div class="k">Risk score</div>
      <div class="v">{{ risk.score }}</div>
      <div class="h">{{ risk.rating }} · weighted {{ risk.weighted_score }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="k">Findings</div>
      <div class="v">{{ summary.findings }}</div>
      <div class="h">{{ severity_counts.critical }} critical · {{ severity_counts.high }} high</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="k">Evidence records</div>
      <div class="v">{{ summary.evidence }}</div>
      <div class="h">hash-on-collection metadata</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="k">Collectors</div>
      <div class="v">{{ summary.collectors.total }}</div>
      <div class="h">
        {% for status, count in summary.collectors.status_counts.items() %}{{ status }}={{ count }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if errors %}
  <div class="callout danger">
    <strong>Collection errors.</strong> {{ errors | length }} collector error(s) were recorded. Review the collector table below; missing data is reported explicitly rather than guessed.
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if warnings %}
  <div class="callout warn" style="margin-top:12px">
    <strong>Collection warnings.</strong> {{ warnings | length }} warning(s) were recorded. These commonly indicate missing privileges, unavailable utilities or absent log sources.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>Executive summary</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        This report records a <strong>read-only</strong> investigation of
        <strong>{{ investigation.hostname }}</strong> ({{ investigation.root }}), executed as
        {{ "root" if investigation.is_root else "an unprivileged user" }}.
        {{ summary.findings }} finding(s) were produced, of which
        {{ severity_counts.critical }} are critical, {{ severity_counts.high }} high,
        {{ severity_counts.medium }} medium, {{ severity_counts.low }} low and
        {{ severity_counts.informational }} informational.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Findings are <strong>indicators, not proof of compromise</strong>. Validate each item
        against change records, package provenance and the asset owner's context before taking
        action. No files were modified, no processes were signalled and no evidence was uploaded.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        Risk formula: <span class="mono">{{ risk.formula }}</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if top_findings %}
  <section>
    <h2>Top findings</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Severity</th><th>Finding</th><th>Collector</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for item in top_findings %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ item.finding_id }}</td>
            <td><span class="badge severity-{{ item.severity }}">{{ item.severity }}</span></td>
            <td>{{ item.title }}<div class="small muted">{{ item.description }}</div></td>
            <td>{{ item.collector }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>Findings by severity</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      {% for severity in severity_order %}
      <div class="card">
        <div class="k">{{ severity }}</div>
        <div class="v" style="color: {{ severity | severity_color }}">{{ severity_counts.get(severity, 0) }}</div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Detailed findings</h2>
    {% if findings %}
      {% for finding in findings %}
      <details class="finding severity-{{ finding.severity }}" {% if finding.severity in ["critical", "high"] %}open{% endif %}>
        <summary>
          <span class="badge severity-{{ finding.severity }}">{{ finding.severity }}</span>
          <span class="title">{{ finding.title }}</span>
          <span class="meta mono">{{ finding.finding_id }}</span>
          <span class="meta">{{ finding.collector }} · {{ finding.detected_at }}</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="body">
          <h4>Observation</h4>
          <p>{{ finding.description }}</p>
          <h4>Why this was flagged</h4>
          <p>{{ finding.why }}</p>
          <h4>False-positive considerations</h4>
          <ul class="chips">
            {% for item in finding.false_positives %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
          <h4>Recommended remediation</h4>
          <p>{{ finding.remediation }}</p>
          <div class="cards" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr)); margin: 14px 0 0;">
            <div><div class="k">Rule</div><div class="mono small">{{ finding.rule_id }}</div></div>
            <div><div class="k">Confidence</div><div class="small">{{ finding.confidence }}</div></div>
            <div><div class="k">Category</div><div class="small">{{ finding.category }}</div></div>
            <div><div class="k">MITRE ATT&amp;CK</div><div class="small">{{ finding.mitre | join(", ") if finding.mitre else "—" }}</div></div>
          </div>
          {% if finding.evidence_refs %}
          <h4>Evidence references</h4>
          <p class="mono small">{{ finding.evidence_refs | join(", ") }}</p>
          {% endif %}
          {% if finding.details %}
          <h4>Details</h4>
          <pre>{{ finding.details | pretty_json }}</pre>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </details>
      {% endfor %}
    {% else %}
      <div class="panel muted">No findings were produced. This does not prove the host is clean: missing privileges, absent logs and unsupported features limit coverage.</div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Collector results</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Collector</th><th>Status</th><th>Duration</th><th>Findings</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Warnings / errors</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for collector in collectors %}
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{{ collector.name }}</strong><div class="small muted">{{ collector.description }}</div></td>
            <td><span class="badge status-{{ collector.status }}">{{ collector.status }}</span></td>
            <td class="mono small">{{ collector.duration_ms }} ms</td>
            <td>{{ collector.finding_ids | length }}</td>
            <td>{{ collector.evidence_ids | length }}</td>
            <td class="small">
              {% for item in collector.errors %}<div class="integrity-bad">{{ item }}</div>{% endfor %}
              {% for item in collector.warnings %}<div class="muted">{{ item }}</div>{% endfor %}
              {% if not collector.errors and not collector.warnings %}—{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Evidence register</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="small muted">
        Evidence is recorded with its source path, collection timestamp and SHA-256 digest where
        hashing is appropriate. Secret-bearing files (for example <code>/etc/shadow</code> and
        private keys) are recorded by metadata only; their content is never copied or digested.
      </p>
      {% if evidence %}
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Kind</th><th>Source / command</th><th>Collected</th><th>SHA-256</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for item in evidence %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ item.evidence_id }}</td>
            <td>{{ item.kind }}</td>
            <td class="mono small">{{ item.source_path or item.command or "—" }}<div class="muted">{{ item.description }}</div></td>
            <td class="mono small">{{ item.collected_at }}</td>
            <td class="mono small">{{ item.sha256 or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="small">{{ item.notes or "—" }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {% else %}
      <p class="muted">No evidence records were produced.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if warnings or errors %}
  <section>
    <h2>Collection diagnostics</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      {% for item in errors %}
      <p><span class="badge status-error">error</span> <strong>{{ item.collector }}</strong>: {{ item.message }}</p>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for item in warnings %}
      <p><span class="badge status-partial">warning</span> <strong>{{ item.collector }}</strong>: {{ item.message }}</p>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>Integrity and methodology</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        <strong>Document integrity:</strong>
        {% if integrity_valid %}
          <span class="integrity-ok">SHA-256 verified</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="integrity-bad">not verified</span>
        {% endif %}
        <span class="mono small">{{ integrity.get("sha256") or "no digest present" }}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">{{ integrity.get("scope") or "" }}</p>
      <p class="small">{{ document.get("methodology", {}).get("description", "") }}</p>
      <p class="small muted">{{ document.methodology.finding_policy }}</p>
      <p class="small muted">
        Redaction: {{ investigation.redaction.note }} Evidence upload: disabled.
        Report rendered at {{ rendered_at }}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Limitations and ethical use</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="small">
        This toolkit is intended for authorised incident response, forensic triage and defensive
        security work only. Obtain explicit written authorisation before examining any system you
        do not own or operate. Findings are observations derived from the state of the host at
        collection time; they can be incomplete, stale or explained by legitimate administration.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        Unprivileged collection cannot see all processes, sockets, logs or account databases.
        Containers, network namespaces, immutable filesystems, tampered binaries and anti-forensic
        activity can all reduce visibility. Absence of a finding is not evidence of integrity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    {{ tool.name }} v{{ tool.version }} · schema {{ tool.schema_version }} ·
    investigation {{ investigation.id }} · generated {{ investigation.generated_at }}
  </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
